  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Choose the incorrect statement:<br />(a) The electric lines of force entering into a Gaussian surface provide negative flux.<br />(b) A charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed at the centre of a cube. The flux through all the faces will be the same.<br />(c) In a uniform electric field net flux through a closed Gaussian surface containing no net charge, is zero.<br />(d) When an electric field is parallel to a Gaussian surface, it provides a finite non-zero flux.</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XRCcq",
      "text": "(b) and (d) Only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DU2Xm",
      "text": "(c) and (d) Only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uBfyD",
      "text": "(a) and (c) Only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FO7W4",
      "text": "(d) Only",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that electric flux is a scalar quantity and this is the scalar product of the magnitude of electric field and surface area.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8b19cb0e-4859-4977-a9d8-eaa0474c2dd1-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 145px;\" /></p><p>Recall, the formula given by Gauss theorem,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, it means,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
